[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169212739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4169212739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4169212739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74gSND","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T10:51:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T10:53:00Z","body":"Not an expert on shaders, so take this with a grain of salt until a core contributor confirms this.\n\nBut I believe you're confusing modulating colors with mixing colors. Modulate multiplies the source color with the desired color, akin to how real lights work. Mixing interpolates the source color with your desired value, shifting it's hue to the target color.\n\nSo the feature is not \"wrong\", only its interpretation.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4169212739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188487250","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4188487250","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4188487250,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75pz5S","user":{"login":"patFTS","id":196640886,"node_id":"U_kgDOC7iAdg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196640886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS","html_url":"https://github.com/patFTS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patFTS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T07:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T16:07:54Z","body":"> Not an expert on shaders, so take this with a grain of salt until a core contributor confirms this.\n> \n> But I believe you're confusing modulating colors with mixing colors. Modulate multiplies the source color with the desired color, akin to how real lights work. Mixing interpolates the source color with your desired value, shifting it's hue to the target color.\n> \n> So the feature is not \"wrong\", only its interpretation.\n\nMan, cant you just do basic visual understanding or something i dont know...?! I mean if you \"modulate\" whatever and set the color to black the image color is fully black... This just gets more stupid everytime, theres just no way. \n\nYour boss ( yellow pikachu there ) is also blending the color... 2 colors black and white...\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188487250/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":2,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"abuse"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188645982","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4188645982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4188645982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75qape","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T10:07:43Z","updated_at":"2026-04-05T10:07:43Z","body":"We have a [Code of Conduct](https://godotengine.org/code-of-conduct/) that must be respected, so please refrain from personal attacks; let's keep the discussion constructive.\n\nI described two mathematical approaches to color calculation: modulation multiplies values, while mixing interpolates values. They are fundamentally different.\n\nAgain, I am not an expert on this topic, so please await for feedback from someone in the rendering team to clarify this.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188645982/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188879079","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4188879079","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4188879079,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75rTjn","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T13:17:35Z","updated_at":"2026-04-06T10:07:06Z","body":"@QbieShay [has confirmed over on RocketChat](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/rendering?msg=SZ89t4yxNsk7iXQjo) that the [modulate is a multiplication](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/canvas_item_shader.html), so this behavior is expected.\n\nSo colors with brightness bigger than 1.0 will naturally \"distort\" the original color towards white. Likewise, modulating any color with black results in black, since in practice you are multiply values by 0.\n\nMixing colors, which is what you intend, can be done with a custom shader, as you demonstrated. The \"...stroke sometimes appears around the image\" is likely a different issue, maybe due to having textures with bilinear filtering.\n\nClosing as not a bug. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188879079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188885168","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4188885168","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4188885168,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc75rVCw","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-05T13:22:22Z","updated_at":"2026-04-06T14:40:17Z","body":"I believe the original post describes an issue with the documentation, which simply says the [modulate colour is “applied”](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_canvasitem.html#class-canvasitem-property-modulate).\n\nThe modulate and self_modulate properties do simply multiply the CanvasItem’s colour with the modulate or self_modulate colour in linear colour encoding. In practice, this means that you can directly modify the relative luminance (the brightness) of a CanvasItem by setting the modulate property to be a greyscale colour (above or below Color.WHITE). When setting the modulate property to be a non-greyscale colour, it will tint the CanvasItem to the modulate colour through a simple linear multiplication operation.\n\n**EDIT:** To anyone who may look into updating the documentation, what I wrote above may only apply to the Mobile/Forward+ renderers. I haven't looked into how the Compatibility renderer behaves and it's possible that this property applies a multiplication operation on nonlinear sRGB-encoded colour values instead of linear-encoded colour values, which would change the behaviour slightly compared to what I described above.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4188885168/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4191576695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117992#issuecomment-4191576695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117992","id":4191576695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc751mJ3","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4",